{# BYTE PARITY IS LOAD-BEARING. On a host where live-restore is not active,
   the notified restart handler bounces every container — so with
   podhaus_docker_live_restore: false this template must render bilby's
   pre-Ansible file exactly: this key order, 2-space indent, trailing
   newline. Any byte drift fires the handler and takes the fleet down.

   The true-render differs from two pre-template files, both acceptably:
   - numbat's on-disk file has the log-opts keys in the other order —
     harmless, because live-restore is already active there and a one-time
     normalising daemon restart doesn't touch containers.
   - fractal's file (written by this role's old inline content) had compact
     one-line log-opts and no live-restore — fractal takes one planned
     handler restart on its next real run and comes out with live-restore.
#}
{
{% if podhaus_docker_live_restore %}
  "live-restore": true,
{% endif %}
  "log-driver": "local",
  "log-opts": {
    "max-size": "50m",
    "max-file": "3"
  }
}
